  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">IWPR Building Resilience through Innovation and Collaboration (BRIC)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">BRIC will advance the goal of strengthening the capacity, collaboration, and effectiveness of local organisations to counter disinformation operations and improve the resilience of the Moldovan public to disinformation, malign influences, and interference from hostile actors. The project will deliver three main objectives: 1) To improve the resilience of Moldovan citizens to disinformation, malign influences, and interference from hostile actors; 2) To strengthen the capacity of Moldovan organisations to counter disinformation, malign influences, and interference from hostile actors; and 3) To strengthen cross-sectoral coordination and collaboration among stakeholders working to counter disinformation, malign influences, and interference from hostile actors.

Under objective 1, IWPR will manage a flexible funding mechanism to support locally-led counter disinformation efforts in Moldova. Funding will prioritise projects that address 1) innovation, 2) community engagement, 3) audience engagement, 4) vulnerable groups, 5) women, with a focus on gendered effects of disinformation, and 6) impact. The primary target groups include 12 Moldovan organisations. The final beneficiaries of the project are the citizens of Moldova, particularly vulnerable audiences.</narrative>
  </description>
